    Fix "Objects are not valid as a React child" error in forms
    
    The application was crashing with a "Runtime Error: Objects are not valid as a React child" because `AddProductForm` and `AddClientForm` were attempting to render `shipping.receiver` directly. The API returns `shipping.receiver` as a full Client object (containing keys like `id`, `client_name`, `total_debts`, etc.) instead of a simple string, causing React to throw an error when trying to render the object.
    
    This commit updates `AddProductForm.tsx` and `AddClientForm.tsx` to conditionally check if `shipping.receiver` is an object. If it is, it renders `shipping.receiver.client_name`; otherwise, it renders the value as-is. This ensures correct rendering of the shipping options in the dropdown menus and prevents the application crash.

